    "readme_excerpt": "# Decentralized Prediction Market ![Solidity](https://img.shields.io/badge/solidity-^0.8.20-blue) ![Type](https://img.shields.io/badge/type-betting-orange) ![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green) ## Overview **Decentralized Prediction Market** allows users to trade on the outcome of future events. This implementation uses a **Parimutuel** betting model: all bets go into a pool, and the winners split the total pool proportional to their share of the winning side. ## How it Works 1. **Create**: Admin (or user) creates a market with a deadline. 2. **Bet**: Users deposit USDC to buy \"YES\" or \"NO\" shares. 3. **Resolve**: An Oracle (or trusted resolver) sets the final outcome. 4. **Claim**: Winners redeem their shares for their portion of the pool. ## Usage ```bash # 1. Install npm install # 2. Deploy Contracts npx hardhat run deploy.js --network localhost # 3. Create a Market (\"Will ETH flip BTC?\") node create_market.js # 4. Place Bets node bet_yes.js node bet_no.js # 5. Resolve Market (Admin only) node resolve.js # 6. Claim Winnings node claim.js",
